From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 14:06:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 352/488] V2 runner: compute selected-token ranks in TileLang

Replace the selected-token rank launch with a TileLang vocabulary scan that
accumulates counts per thread and reduces once per row, rather than once
per 8192-element chunk. Prepare its dtype/stride and token-ID variants at
startup through the existing TileLang registry. The Triton kernel remains
only as the test and benchmark reference; remove its dispatcher and warmup.

Base: release-next 174a746f4577579841e5aa3e94c8a4964b0aa326 (candidate 4).
Rank semantics, including ties, NaNs and the old -inf padding behaviour,
are unchanged. This reports integer ranks and changes no model arithmetic,
probabilities or sampled tokens. No runtime fallback or new backend flag.
Upstream status: local DS41F fork experiment; not submitted upstream.

Validation on DGX Spark/GB10, candidate-4 image: 24 focused GPU tests pass,
24 pass under compute-sanitizer with 0 memory errors. Two paired 15-shape
performance runs at vocabulary 129280 pass without a slower case. FP32 at
one row: ~7.7 us vs ~16.9 us; at 16 rows: ~8.3 us vs ~17.3 us. The 96-row
FP32 case is bandwidth-bound and level (about 168 us). 256 threads for FP32,
512 for FP16/BF16, chosen by the recorded 128/256/512-thread sweep. Lowered
and nvcc-compiled offline for sm_121a; Ruff and diff checks pass.
